# Copilot and Cursor Rules for Airose Studio

## General Understanding
- The site is a static React application built with Webpack.
- All dynamic content is stored in /data in JSON files.
- Local editing uses Webpack dev-server FS routes under /dev/*.
- Production editing is disabled.
- Publishing uses scripts/publish.ts to commit updated JSON to GitHub.

## When writing code:
- Prefer using the new persistence layer under src/lib/persistence.
- Prefer the `Result<T>` pattern and unified httpPost/httpGet wrappers.
- Avoid using axios (project standard is native fetch).
- Use /dev/sections/save for sections-based content.
- Always ensure buttons in editors use type="button" to avoid page reloads.
- When suggesting edits, maintain Vercel static-compatibility.

## When uncertain:
- Copilot should check docs/architecture.md for system rules.
- Copilot should not guess backend APIs; instead use the Webpack dev routes.
- Copilot should always assume Editor Mode is local-only.
